The second script is preferable because it  

• uses built‑in date functions (EXTRACT/QUARTER) instead of a manual SUBSTR, making the logic clearer and less error‑prone if the date format ever changes;  
• filters the data to 2013 in the same step that calculates the invoice totals, so unnecessary rows from other years are never materialised;  
• produces the same numeric result while remaining fully readable and standards‑compliant.  

